# The clipboard strip where the on-screen keyboard leaves too little room for the field and a 7 mm strip (640x480: about 120 px
# above the keyboard, 480x320: about 80): the pills shrink to what is left (never under 32 px, text scaled with them), the label
# above the field goes while they do, and the strip is fully visible above the keyboard (expect_strip checks it). The buttons work
# and the keyboard stays. When the keyboard goes the strip is 7 mm again. Review only.
title clipboard strip with the keyboard, shrunk pills
review
sizes 640x480 480x320
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env APPLAUNCH_OSK force
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
clipboard server on
clipboard set "from elsewhere"
fielddemo
wait 800
expect_osk shown
expect_strip Name paste=on copy=on clear=on editing=yes size=tight
shot osk_strip_tight
tapclip Name Copy
expect_strip Name copy_text=Copied editing=yes size=tight
expect_osk shown
shot osk_strip_tight_copied
tapclip Name Clear
expect_strip Name copy=off clear=hide editing=yes size=tight
tapclip Name Paste
expect_field Name "café €5 and more"
expect_osk shown
# the password field: Paste and Clear
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
expect_strip Secret paste=on copy=hide clear=on editing=yes size=tight
shot osk_strip_tight_password
# the keyboard goes (Esc ends the editing): the label and the 7 mm come back for the next field
key ESC
expect_osk hidden
